uot;, is a grammar of the Kannada language written by the poet Kesiraja around 1260, in the Hoysala period.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/shabwa"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/shabwa.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Shabwa</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Shabwa was the capital of the ancient Kingdom of Hadramawt, on the edge of the desert in what is now southern Yemen.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/shackamaxon"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/shackamaxon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Shackamaxon</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Shackamaxon was a Lenape settlement on the Delaware River, in what is now the Fishtown district of Philadelphia.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/shadegan"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/shadegan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Shadegan</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Shadegan, formerly Fallahiyeh, is a town in Khuzestan province in south-western Iran, near the large Shadegan wetlands at the head of the Persian Gulf.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/shafii-school"><span class="enc-name">Shafi'i school</span><span class="enc-type">Religion / idea</span><span class="enc-snip">The Shafi'i school is one of the four major schools of Sunni Islamic law, named after the jurist al-Shafi'i.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/shaftesbury"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/shaftesbury.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Shaftesbury</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Shaftesbury is a hilltop town in north Dorset, England.</span></a></li><li clas